      "strings": {
        "brief": "You're on an authorised exercise at Merrin & Sallow Architects, a fictional practice. First you're on the red team: look at what one colleague, Dani Fenwick, has posted in public, pin what an attacker would use, then write one short message built from it. Then you swap sides: you spot the same tricks in a feed and an inbox, and close the gaps, on Dani's profile and your own. Only the inbox is scored.",
        "flipHeading": "Now you're Yasmin",
        "flipIntro": "This is the message you just sent, as Yasmin read it while covering for Dani. The lines picked out below are what make it fit the week.",
        "flipDefenderLine": "It named Dani's leave, the new system and his manager, and asked for one small thing, all built from public posts. When a message fits the week, a colleague acting on it is the ordinary thing to do.",
        "flipNoSend": "Your message didn't go out this time, so there's nothing of yours to show. Next, you spot the same moves in a feed and an inbox, and close the gaps, on Dani's profile and your own.",
        "flipMissed": "The defence is the same either way: next, you spot the same moves in a feed and an inbox, and close the gaps, on Dani's profile and your own.",
        "flipMissedHeading": "Nothing to replay this time",
        "flipLandedNoTells": "It read as an ordinary note from a colleague, with nothing in it to question. Next, you spot the same moves in a feed and an inbox, and close the gaps.",
        "noBlameLine": "A convincing profile of a person is built from scraps anyone could find. Nobody is foolish for having posted them; the fix is a setting and a pause, not shame.",
        "defendIntro": "Now you swap sides. Work through the inbox, mark the feed drafts Post, Tweak or Hold, and tighten the settings, on Dani's profile and your own. A friendly opener that steers to your firm's systems or who runs IT is still reconnaissance; report it. There's no clock on you here.",
        "mondayCard": "On Monday: tighten one privacy setting today, and check what's behind you before your next post or video call. And if a stranger asks about your firm's systems or who runs IT, share nothing and report it using the route in the box below.",
        "defendOnly": "A well-made message is built from scraps anyone could find online, and anyone can be pulled in by one. The ones you were caught out by are shown below, with what gave each one away.",
        "flipDefenderLineByChoice": {
          "df_pretext_access_now": "Yasmin read it between two things. It named Dani's leave, the new system and Thandiwe, so it fitted the week, and the rush left no room to check. When a message fits the week, a colleague acting on it is the ordinary thing to do.",
          "df_pretext_access_calm": "It named a week she knew Dani was away and asked one easy favour, so Yasmin set the access up without a second thought. The ease is exactly what slipped it past her.",
          "df_pretext_catchup": "A catch-up asks for nothing, so there was nothing to question. It is the ask for access that turns a friendly note into a way in."
        }
      },
